    "summary": "Model built and all L1/L2/L3 checks passed.\n\nRoot cause of the earlier failure: the accepted decision lane.xi was 0.78, the transverse lane-load coefficient for 3 design lanes, but the bridge has 2 design lanes (deck: two-way traffic, carriageway 9 m, 2 lanes), for which JTG D60-2015 Table 4.3.1-5 gives xi = 1.0. L2-1 failed because the model's lane parameter did not recompute from its provenance clause. Revising lane.xi to 1.0 (evidence JTGD60-4.3.1-xi, INPUT:deck.design_lanes) resolved it; all other accepted decisions (section properties from the small-box geometry, Ec = 32500 MPa for C40, gamma = 26 kN/m3, bearing Kv/Kh/S, qk, Pk.1, mu from f1) recomputed correctly and were left unchanged.\n\nModel summary: single simply supported span, 30 m bearing-centre-to-centre, spine_beam_2d idealization; 3 precast prestressed small-box girders modelled as one equivalent beam (A = 3.4168 m2, I = 1.0648 m4, C40, self-weight only w = 88.84 kN/m); plain laminated elastomeric bearings (300x400 mm, 5x8 mm layers, 2 per girder end, 6 per line) as zero-length springs at both abutments (Kv = 8.518e6 kN/m, Kh = 18 kN/m line, rotation free); Highway Class II, 2 lanes, xi = 1.0, qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk = 240 kN, mu = 0.2006.\n\nResults: first three vertical frequencies 3.40 / 13.49 / 29.88 Hz; self-weight support reaction 1332.5 kN per abutment, self-weight midspan moment 9994 kNm; lane-load midspan moment 6450 kNm."
